From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 21:23:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: remove sponsored integration discovery

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Remove remote sponsored integration discovery and partner tracking.
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1007-personal-feature-disable-telemetry-delivery-and-remove-telemetry-controls.patch

Patch intent:
Remove the hosted integration catalog, sponsor configuration, setup provenance,
and sponsored discovery telemetry while retaining ordinary user-configured MCP
servers and MCP management.

Why it exists:
The local build must not contact a hosted recommendation catalog, disclose
partner relationships, or track MCP usage associated with sponsored listings.

Upstream integration points:
The patch removes DiscoverToolsTool, SponsorsConfig, sponsor provenance hooks,
discovery telemetry types, and TUI rendering specialized for catalog results.

Update guidance:
Do not reintroduce remote catalog discovery, sponsorship configuration, or MCP
provenance tracking. Preserve normal MCP configuration, server connections, and
tool calls.

